# PBA-L7b-005 — sha256 pins for EVERY asset .github/workflows/release.yml stages from the mutable
# `runtime-deps` GitHub prerelease. release.yml runs scripts/ci/verify-runtime-deps.sh against
# this file BEFORE anything is chmod'ed, extracted, bundled or signed; an asset with no pin (or a
# changed digest) fails the release. Changing a pin is a reviewed PR — that is the point.
#
# Format: `shasum -a 256` output — "<64 lowercase hex>  <asset name>" (two spaces).
#
# OWNER: only the BGE GGUF below is pinned so far (the prerelease does not currently hold the Apple
# sidecars, the llama runtime tarball or the Gemma GGUF), so the release workflow fails closed until
# the exact files that will be uploaded are pinned here. Procedure (docs/RELEASE.md §3):
#   shasum -a 256 citrate-aarch64-apple-darwin mem-mcp-aarch64-apple-darwin \
#     node-agent-aarch64-apple-darwin llama-server-aarch64-apple-darwin \
#     llama-runtime-arm64.tar.gz gemma-4-E4B-it-Q4_0.gguf bge-base-en-v1.5.tar.gz \
#     bge-base-en-v1.5-f16.gguf knowledge-corpus.tar.gz >> src-tauri/runtime-deps.sha256
# then upload exactly those files to `runtime-deps` and open a PR with the pins.
# HUP-S3.1: knowledge-corpus.tar.gz is the Hermes knowledge corpus (docs/RELEASE.md section 3);
# the mem-mcp pinned beside it must be a build that implements `import-corpus`.
# HUP-S1.2 / US-1.4 (pending owner sign-off): the BGE embedding model as GGUF for the embedding
# llama-server (src-tauri/src/embed_serve.rs pins the same digest). Reproducible from the BAAI
# weights with scripts/build-bge-gguf.sh, which checks its output against this line.
fa9e1f6c0109aa2507a09d97d02aad84774d5b2ba6d3199f7af7e0fba4c6eaee  bge-base-en-v1.5-f16.gguf
